My name is TTP. 

I was born with neurological impairment/challenges, quadra para plegic, diagonosed later as mixed cerebral palsy. It affects every cell of my body and crippled them.

A key feature of it is the impact it has on your informational processing systems. How you process information in your brain and the rest of your body and your body sends information back.

So by that standard, I should be a dumbass, I should be invalid. I never really had a chance did I?

Instead I was given the oppurtunity to know life. To celebrate the struggle, the joy, and the sadness with my mental health. I bear it on the greatest stage of any universe, in a spotlight, under scrunity, and I invite all those who are willing to join me. 

Mind over Muscule. Spirit over Body. I was called upon to re-set my neuro logistical pathways on the cell by cell level. I was forced to gain the ability of rapid adaptativity.

I have read since 1989. It is one of my favorite hobbies.

I have programmed/written things in one form or another since 1989. All on a desperate quest to be a computer game developer.

Every generation has a version of the TTP crew. The membership has changed throughout time, both growing and shrinking. They have seen me through the best and worst times of my entire life.

Every generation I love them more & more, and they mean more and more to me.

On this site you will find collections of writings, mainly about video games but I do try to cover other topics and other areas of interest. 

I have a big interest in reading and writing human interest stories and things that can serve to inspire myself and others.

You will find a library of self-created video games by myself. You will find coverage of several friends projects as well.

